 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to the qualification to\nhold the position of assistant district attorney in the county of Rensselaer",
    "basePrintNo": "S5962",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5962-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5962\n\nSPONSOR: ASHBY\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo Permit residents of Rensselaer county and adjoining counties to hold\nthe position of Assistant District Attorney in Rensselaer county.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends public officers law by adding a new subdivision that\nauthorizes residents of counties which adjoin Rensselaer County to serve\nas Assistant District Attorney in Rensselaer County. This provision does\nnot apply to the position of chief assistant district attorney.\n\nSection 2: Sets effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill has been introduced at the request of the Rensselaer County\nDistrict Attorney's Office. This legislation will allow Rensselaer Coun-\nty to expand its pool of eligible applicants and be able hire qualified\nindividuals from adjacent counties to hold the position of Assistant\nDistrict Attorney in Rensselaer County. Similar authorizations have been\nprovided to multiple counties around NYS.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
